      "answer": {
        "schema_version": "grounded-answer-v1",
        "answer_id": "ans_f8ba5b07f51a4065bef25b862db6cbd6",
        "run_id": "run_8218854a3e454bff8580cf0171341495",
        "answer_markdown": "The predictor flags hERG as a concern: Compound X is classified as a **blocker**, with a model score of **0.6803638935089111**. This is an uncalibrated model score, not a clinical risk estimate.\n\nPrioritize:\n- Direct hERG patch-clamp confirmation with concentration-response, using the free-drug exposure range anticipated in development.\n- A broader cardiac ion-channel panel and action-potential assay if hERG activity is confirmed.\n- Early PK and exposure-margin work, followed by in vivo QT/ECG assessment only if the in vitro signal persists at relevant exposures.\n- Medicinal-chemistry profiling of close analogues to reduce hERG activity while retaining the desired pharmacology.\n\nThe model’s applicability status is **ok**, but this is only an element-composition rule and does not establish distributional similarity. These experiments are screening and follow-up risk characterization, not a safety assessment.",
        "claims": [
          {
            "claim_id": "clm_8f42a7c19d6e4b03a5c1f9e7d2b6c8a4",
            "kind": "classification",
            "text": "The hERG predictor classifies Compound X as a blocker.",
            "transform": "identity",
            "citation_ids": [],
            "observation_id": "obs_3b9246b0fe7d48dbada04f107f1f4772",
            "field_path": "predictions.herg.label",
            "source_value": "blocker"
          },
          {
            "claim_id": "clm_2d7e9a4c6b1f8e03a5d9c2b7f4a6e1d8",
